  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 236 PM MST WED NOV 11 2026\nwill continue to move through the region and then east Saturday,\nwith lingering precipitation ending gradually through the day \nbehind the cold front. Winds will also remain breezy behind the\nfront and gradually weaken in the evening. A brief upper-level\nridge will make an appearance Sunday, creating dry and slightly\nwarmer conditions from Saturday. The next system will be fast \napproaching late Sunday as a deep upper-level trough moves inland\nfrom the Gulf of Alaska. Winds will increase yet again late Sunday\ninto early next week as this pattern moves in. This trough will\nalso weaken as it moves over the area while still bringing a cold\nfront and precipitation. While ensembles differ on the exact \ntiming, it is expected to move through between Sunday night and \nearly Tuesday, with Monday seeing the highest (50-80%) chances of \nprecipitation.  Light to locally moderate precipitation totals\nare expected. Snow levels will lower from around 6000 feet Sunday\nnight to 4000-5500 feet by the time precipitation ends, allowing\nfor additional mountain snowfall. Temperatures will trend lower\nwith highs cooling to near normal by Tuesday. Winds will continue\nto weaken as the system progresses but remain locally breezy. \n\nOn Wednesday, another low from the Gulf of Alaska will approach\nthe coast with precipitation chances increasing late in the day.",
